{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XJjAr3iy3SjCkjiDG6fMJM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd111-ptx\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/ptx: Produce a Permuted Index\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS does not ship ptx. GNU ptx produces a permuted (keyword-in-context) index of\n6\t  text input. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gptx,\n7\t  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n8\t\n9\tgoals:\n10\t  - G1: Produce a permuted (KWIC) index from text input.\n11\t  - G2: Support output width, gap size, and reference control.\n12\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gptx via differential testing.\n13\t\n14\trequirements:\n15\t  R1:\n16\t    title: KWIC index generation\n17\t    items:\n18\t      - R1.1:\n19\t          text: Must read input lines and produce a permuted index where each significant word appears as a keyword in context, with the surrounding text shown on either side.\n20\t\n21\t  R2:\n22\t    title: Index options\n23\t    items:\n24\t      - R2.1:\n25\t          text: \"-w N or --width=N must set the output line width (default 72). -g N or --gap-size=N must set the minimum gap between columns (default 3).\"\n26\t      - R2.2:\n27\t          text: \"-f or --ignore-case must fold lowercase to uppercase for sorting purposes.\"\n28\t      - R2.3:\n29\t          text: Must read from FILE or stdin when no file or \"-\" is given.\n30\t\n31\t  R3:\n32\t    title: Word regexp\n33\t    items:\n34\t      - R3.1:\n35\t          text: \"-W REGEXP or --word-regexp=REGEXP must use REGEXP to define what constitutes a word.\"\n36\t\n37\t  R4:\n38\t    title: Reference control\n39\t    items:\n40\t      - R4.1:\n41\t          text: \"-A or --auto-reference must produce automatically generated references based on file name and line number.\"\n42\t      - R4.2:\n43\t          text: \"-r or --references must treat the first field of each line as a reference and exclude it from the index.\"\n44\t\n45\t  R5:\n46\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n47\t    items:\n48\t      - R5.1:\n49\t          text: Must exit 0 on success. Must exit 1 on any error.\n50\t      - R5.2:\n51\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n52\t\n53\tnon_goals:\n54\t  - cmd/ptx does not implement TeX/roff output format in this release.\n55\t\n56\tacceptance_criteria:\n57\t  - id: AC1\n58\t    criterion: \"ptx on a text file produces a permuted index, matching gptx.\"\n59\t    traces:\n60\t      - R1.1\n61\t      - R2.3\n62\t  - id: AC2\n63\t    criterion: \"ptx -f folds case for sorting, matching gptx -f.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R2.2\n66\t  - id: AC3\n67\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gptx passes.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R1.1\n70\t  - id: AC4\n71\t    criterion: \"cmd/ptx compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n72\t    traces:\n73\t      - R1.1\n74\t      - R2.1\n75\t      - R2.2\n76\t      - R2.3\n77\t      - R3.1\n78\t      - R4.1\n79\t      - R4.2\n80\t      - R5.1\n81\t      - R5.2\n82\t\n83\tpackage_contract:\n84\t  imports:\n85\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n86\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KCaPKea3kPGT6hj8ohzrFv","session_id":"92eb9d44-3100-4344-b576-e8e69ede5b06","uuid":"3e63493b-eab4-4aac-8424-18c86043aaac","timestamp":"2026-05-30T16:39:53.568Z"}
