{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KCaPKea3kPGT6hj8ohzrFv","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are the complete contents of all three files:\n\n## 1. SRD111-PTX Specification (srd111-ptx.yaml)\n\nThe specification defines requirements for implementing a permuted (KWIC) index tool to match GNU ptx behavior. Key sections:\n\n**R5 - Exit codes and SIGPIPE (the requirements you specifically requested):**\n- **R5.1:** Must exit 0 on success. Must exit 1 on any error.\n- **R5.2:** Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\n**Full context for ptx behavior:**\n- **R1:** KWIC index generation - reads input lines and produces a permuted index where each significant word appears as a keyword in context\n- **R2:** Index options including width (-w, default 72), gap size (-g, default 3), ignore-case (-f), and file/stdin reading\n- **R3:** Word regexp support (-W) to define what constitutes a word\n- **R4:** Reference control with auto-reference (-A) and explicit references (-r)\n\nAcceptance criteria AC4 requires the tool compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint and must trace all requirements including R5.1 and R5.2.\n\n## 2. Main Implementation (main.go)\n\nComplete Go implementation with:\n\n**SIGPIPE handling:**\n- Line 57: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` called at program start\n- Lines 76-82: Error handling in `writeOutput()` explicitly checks for `syscall.EPIPE` and exits with code 0 if detected\n- Line 78: `os.Exit(0)` on EPIPE (graceful exit as required by R5.2)\n\n**Exit codes:**\n- Line 62: `os.Exit(1)` on argument parsing errors\n- Line 68: `os.Exit(1)` on file reading errors  \n- Lines 77-81: `os.Exit(0)` on EPIPE, `os.Exit(1)` on other write errors\n\n**Core functionality:**\n- Flag parsing for all R2-R4 options (width, gap-size, ignore-case, word-regexp, auto-reference, references)\n- Input reading from files or stdin\n- KWIC index building with word span detection\n- Sorting by sort key (with optional case folding)\n- Formatted output with proper spacing and reference columns\n\n## 3. Test File (ptx_test.go)\n\nDifferential testing suite using `testutils.DiffTest`:\n\n**Test coverage:**\n- Basic KWIC index generation from stdin\n- Empty input handling\n- Width flag variations (-w, --width=, --width, -w50)\n- Gap-size flag variations (-g, --gap-size=, -g5)\n- Ignore-case functionality (-f, --ignore-case)\n- Case-sensitive sorting without -f\n- File input with explicit stdin dash (-)\n- Combined flags (-fw50)\n\nAll tests compare Go implementation output byte-for-byte against the reference `gptx` binary. The test file currently tests requirements R2.1, R2.2, and R2.3 (file reading), but does not yet include tests for R3 (word-regexp), R4 (references/auto-reference), or R5 (exit codes/SIGPIPE)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92eb9d44-3100-4344-b576-e8e69ede5b06","uuid":"5670c635-6a4a-4244-a93f-06a0958f1fb7","timestamp":"2026-05-30T16:40:04.645Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to read three files in detail. Please read each one fully:\n\n1. /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5675/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd111-ptx.yaml - I need specifically the R5 requirement group (R5.1 and R5.2), but also any context from the rest of the SRD that helps understand ptx behavior.\n\n2. /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5675/cmd/ptx/main.go - The full existing implementation\n\n3. /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5675/cmd/ptx/ptx_test.go - The full existing test file\n\nPlease return the complete contents of all three files.","agentId":"a228ad1e736e98ce3","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are the complete contents of all three files:\n\n## 1. SRD111-PTX Specification (srd111-ptx.yaml)\n\nThe specification defines requirements for 