{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lx5XBYpzpfetBHzbPEAahW","type":"tool_result","content":"0\tid: srd111-ptx\n1\ttitle: \"cmd/ptx: Produce a Permuted Index\"\n2\t\n3\tproblem: |\n4\t  macOS does not ship ptx. GNU ptx produces a permuted (keyword-in-context) index of\n5\t  text input. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gptx,\n6\t  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n7\t\n8\tgoals:\n9\t  - G1: Produce a permuted (KWIC) index from text input.\n10\t  - G2: Support output width, gap size, and reference control.\n11\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gptx via differential testing.\n12\t\n13\trequirements:\n14\t  R1:\n15\t    title: KWIC index generation\n16\t    items:\n17\t      - R1.1:\n18\t          text: Must read input lines and produce a permuted index where each significant word appears as a keyword in context, with the surrounding text shown on either side.\n19\t\n20\t  R2:\n21\t    title: Index options\n22\t    items:\n23\t      - R2.1:\n24\t          text: \"-w N or --width=N must set the output line width (default 72). -g N or --gap-size=N must set the minimum gap between columns (default 3).\"\n25\t      - R2.2:\n26\t          text: \"-f or --ignore-case must fold lowercase to uppercase for sorting purposes.\"\n27\t      - R2.3:\n28\t          text: Must read from FILE or stdin when no file or \"-\" is given.\n29\t\n30\t  R3:\n31\t    title: Word regexp\n32\t    items:\n33\t      - R3.1:\n34\t          text: \"-W REGEXP or --word-regexp=REGEXP must use REGEXP to define what constitutes a word.\"\n35\t\n36\t  R4:\n37\t    title: Reference control\n38\t    items:\n39\t      - R4.1:\n40\t          text: \"-A or --auto-reference must produce automatically generated references based on file name and line number.\"\n41\t      - R4.2:\n42\t          text: \"-r or --references must treat the first field of each line as a reference and exclude it from the index.\"\n43\t\n44\t  R5:\n45\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n46\t    items:\n47\t      - R5.1:\n48\t          text: Must exit 0 on success. Must exit 1 on any error.\n49\t      - R5.2:\n50\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n51\t\n52\tnon_goals:\n53\t  - cmd/ptx does not implement TeX/roff output format in this release.\n54\t\n55\tacceptance_criteria:\n56\t  - id: AC1\n57\t    criterion: \"ptx on a text file produces a permuted index, matching gptx.\"\n58\t    traces:\n59\t      - R1.1\n60\t      - R2.3\n61\t  - id: AC2\n62\t    criterion: \"ptx -f folds case for sorting, matching gptx -f.\"\n63\t    traces:\n64\t      - R2.2\n65\t  - id: AC3\n66\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gptx passes.\"\n67\t    traces:\n68\t      - R1.1\n69\t  - id: AC4\n70\t    criterion: \"cmd/ptx compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n71\t    traces:\n72\t      - R1.1\n73\t      - R2.1\n74\t      - R2.2\n75\t      - R2.3\n76\t      - R3.1\n77\t      - R4.1\n78\t      - R4.2\n79\t      - R5.1\n80\t      - R5.2\n81\t\n82\tpackage_contract:\n83\t  imports:\n84\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92eb9d44-3100-4344-b576-e8e69ede5b06","uuid":"ffd14ed2-d06e-481b-b79e-059f3869cf96","timestamp":"2026-05-30T16:41:07.710Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5675/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd111-ptx.yaml","content":"id: srd111-ptx\ntitle: \"cmd/ptx: Produce a Permuted Index\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS does not ship ptx. GNU ptx produces a permuted (keyword-in-context) index of\n  text input. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gptx,\n  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Produce a permuted (KWIC) index from text input.\n  - G2: Support output width, gap size, and reference control.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gptx via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: KWIC index generation\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must read input lines and produce a permuted index where each significant word appears as a keyword in context, with the surrounding text shown on either side.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Index options\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-w N or --width=N must set the output line width (default 72). -g N or --gap-size=N must set the minimum gap between columns (default 3).\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-f or --ignore-case must fold lowercase to uppercase for sorting purposes.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must read from FILE or stdin when no file or \"-\" is given.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Word regexp\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-W REGEXP or --word-regexp=REGEXP must use REGEXP to define what constitutes a word.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Reference control\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: \"-A or --auto-reference must produce automatically generated references based on file name and line number.\"\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"-r or --references must treat the first field of each line as a reference and exclude it from the index.\"\n\n  R5:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R5.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 on success. Must exit 1 on any error.\n      - R5.2:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/ptx does not implement TeX/roff output format in this release.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"ptx on a text file produces a permuted index, matching gptx.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"ptx -f folds case for sorting, matching gptx -f.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gptx passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/ptx compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R5.1\n      - R5.2\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":86,"startLine":0,"totalLines":86}}}
